622 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Contact is a sci\055fi novel about humanity establishing communication with an alien civilization\056 A crucial plot point is that humans discover the alien species uses an entirely different information system\054 one beyond familiar language\054 symbols\054 or logic\056 Deciphering this nonhuman perception becomes a core challenge in understanding extraterrestrial intelligence\056\n\nThis concept made me realize that many literary and cinematic works\054 as well as real\055world scientific initiatives concerning contact with extraterrestrial life\054 revolve around the same fundamental question\072 how can we overcome the limitations of human perception and cognition to understand different forms of life\077\n\nIt also made me realize that the challenge of communicating with aliens reflects a broader issue\072 as humans\054 we shape the Earth based on our own perceptions while often neglecting the environments of other species\056 Anthropocentrism leads us to see human perception as the default\054 marginalizing the needs and sensory experiences of other life forms\056)
     /K [ 6 ]
     /P 623 0 R
     /Pg 610 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

