628 0 obj
  << /ActualText (The Anthropocene is a concept in geology and environmental studies that refers to the profound and irreversible impact of human activities on Earth\047s ecosystems\054 to the extent that it defines a new geological epoch\056\n\nFirst proposed by atmospheric chemist Paul Crutzen in 2000\054 the term highlights how industrialization\054 urban expansion\054 climate change\054 and biodiversity loss are reshaping the global environment\056\n\nDiscussions of the Anthropocene are often intertwined with post\055anthropocentric thought\054 as the concept challenges the notion of humans as separate from nature\054 instead positioning them as just one among many species deeply embedded within Earth\047s systems\056)
     /K [ 9 ]
     /P 629 0 R
     /Pg 610 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

